# What EAS Build uploads. Mirrors .gitignore, with one deliberate exception:
# google-services.json IS uploaded.
#
# app.json points `android.googleServicesFile` at ./google-services.json, but
# that file is gitignored, so the build archive never contained it and EAS
# failed during prebuild ("...won't be uploaded to the builder"). It holds the
# Firebase project id and FCM sender id — needed at build time for the app to
# obtain a push token at all — and is not a secret in the way a service-account
# key is. gsa.json (the actual service-account credential) stays excluded.

node_modules/

.expo/
dist/
web-build/

*.orig.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision

.metro-health-check*

npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*

.DS_Store
*.pem

.env*.local

*.tsbuildinfo

# Native projects are regenerated by prebuild on the builder.
android/
ios/

expo-env.d.ts

.vscode
.claude
graphify-out/
CLAUDE.md

gsa.json
